course: dictionary
lesson: 2391
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. A currant can be a small dried grape, or a small round berry that grows in bunches on a bush.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A glass box under the table holds a small cake with "EAT ME" marked in currants» is about a cake, so the currants are the small dried grapes that go in cakes. A bush full of berries would fit a garden, but not a cake.
explain: Test each meaning in the sentence. Does "a cake marked in small dried grapes" make sense? Yes. Does "a cake marked in berries on a bush" make sense? No, so the first meaning fits.
fact: Currant means a small dried black grape without seeds, used in cakes, buns and puddings.
fact: Currant also means a small round berry that grows in bunches on a bush, such as blackcurrant, redcurrant and whitecurrant.
fact: «Five currant buns in a baker's shop» is a nursery rhyme, and the currants are the dried grapes in the buns.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, a little cake marked «EAT ME» is made with currants.
fact: Blackcurrant juice is popular in the UK.
exercise: What is a currant in «He made one cake from flour, water, currants, plums and sugar»? | *A small dried black grape used in cakes | A type of flour | A small round berry that grows on a bush | A plum with a stone inside
exercise: «Blackcurrant juice is popular in the UK.» What is a blackcurrant? | *A small round berry that grows in bunches on a bush | A small dried grape for buns | A large yellow fruit from a tree | A kind of sugar
exercise: In «a small cake with "EAT ME" marked in currants», which word tells you the currants are food? | *cake | under | glass | table
test: In «Five currant buns in a baker's shop», which meaning of currant fits? | A bunch of flowers | A shop sign | *A small dried black grape used in buns | A small round berry on a bush in a garden
test: In «old, dry, stale cake-crumbs and some burned currants», what are the currants? | *Small dried grapes that were baked into cake | Dry leaves from a tree | Crumbs of bread from a loaf | A kind of hat
exam: Which is NOT a meaning of currant? | A small dried black grape used in buns | *A large green apple that grows on a tree | A small round berry that grows in bunches on a bush
